  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "The final S2 removes any sales stop above 5%, making the threshold a trigger for corrective action only, which is the main weakening and the largest benefit to Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%). S5 keeps the 8/100k mandatory recall with no transition, which exposes Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9/100k), while S4's 36-month suppression deadline and S3's 6-year retrofit fall within acceptable ranges. Per-model results go to purchasers and regulators, but not to the public, which preserves the customer-access red line."
 },
